          <msContents>
            <summary>Book containing a number of receipts, descriptions of diseases and remedies. This manuscript is the author's holograph.</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="it" source="IANA">Italian</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_174_1">
              <author>Cagali, Gasparo Di</author>
              <title type="original">Libro di ricette medicinali</title>
              <textLang mainLang="it" source="IANA">Italian, in the Verona dialect.</textLang>
              <note>Inside the cover notes of his personal affairs beginning 'Questo libero sie di Mº. gasparo barbiro e ceroicho che fu fiolo di mº antonio ceroicho da Legnago di chagalii habito in la contra di S. Zen...e questo libro fu scritto adi 15 agosto 1529...' </note>
              <note>Ef. 24v-32 contain a Latin-Italian list of the names of herbs.</note>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
          <physDesc>
            <objectDesc form="codex">
              <supportDesc material="perg"><extent>3 ll. +75 ff. 8vo.
                <dimensions type="leaf" unit="cm">
                  <dim type="width">11.5 cm</dim>
                  <dim type="length">17.5 cm</dim>
                </dimensions>
              </extent>
                <condition><p></p></condition>
              </supportDesc>
            </objectDesc>
            <decoDesc>
              <decoNote type="illustration">On the cover a pen-drawn coat of arms of the writer. </decoNote>
              <decoNote type="illustration"> Inside the lower cover two drawings of distilling apparatus. </decoNote>
              <decoNote type="marginal">Illustrated by several small marginal pen-drawings of diseased organs, instruments, etc. </decoNote>
            </decoDesc>
            <bindingDesc>
              <binding>
                <p>Original vellum binding, with leather ties, one wanting.</p>
              </binding>
            </bindingDesc>
          </physDesc>
          <history>
            <origin>
              <origDate>1529</origDate>
            </origin>
            <provenance>On the verso of the last leaf is a note of the birth and baptism, in 1530 at Verona, of the Author's son 'Zuan Antonio'. In the inscription inside the upper cover, the birth of a daughter 'Chatalina' on 14 November 1527 is mentioned.  Produced in Verona.</provenance>
            <acquisition>Purchased from Davis and Orioli, 28 August 1928 (accession 48527).</acquisition>
          </history>
